body:
> Are there already functions to escape strings that could be used to pre-process `user` here?

I think vim_mktempdir should just replace slashes when it is building the path. Can use `memchrsub`. Can you try this patch, then yes a PR would be great!

```
diff --git a/src/nvim/fileio.c b/src/nvim/fileio.c
index febde53ce2c3..251e658980e8 100644
--- a/src/nvim/fileio.c
+++ b/src/nvim/fileio.c
@@ -5296,6 +5296,11 @@ static void vim_mktempdir(void)
   char user[40] = { 0 };
 
   (void)os_get_username(user, sizeof(user));
+  // Usernames may contain slashes! #19240
+  memchrsub(user, PATHSEP, '_', sizeof(user));
+#ifdef BACKSLASH_IN_FILENAME
+  memchrsub(user, psepcN, '_', sizeof(user));
+#endif
 
   // Make sure the umask doesn't remove the executable bit.
   // "repl" has been reported to use "0177".
```

you can skip `make install` and just use `./build/bin/nvim` after `make`.

try this patch instead:

```diff
diff --git a/src/nvim/fileio.c b/src/nvim/fileio.c
index febde53ce2c3..251e658980e8 100644
--- a/src/nvim/fileio.c
+++ b/src/nvim/fileio.c
@@ -5296,6 +5296,11 @@ static void vim_mktempdir(void)
   char user[40] = { 0 };
 
   (void)os_get_username(user, sizeof(user));
+  // Usernames may contain slashes! #19240
+  memchrsub(user, '/', '_', sizeof(user));
+  memchrsub(user, '\\', '_', sizeof(user));
 
   // Make sure the umask doesn't remove the executable bit.
   // "repl" has been reported to use "0177".
```

> You think the second patch is a viable solution @justinmk? If so, I'm happy to throw that in a PR with some tests and submit it.

@levouh yes, thanks! A test would be great but might be difficult to get working in CI, especially on Windows. idk a way to force a user name. would be easier if we used os_homedir but that should probably be a separate PR. 

can skip the test  if it's too much trouble.
